-- title:
--   Finiteness of supersingular places of the modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $N$ be natural numbers with $N \neq 0$ and $q$ prime, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$. Consider the level-$N$ geometric modular function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\ K\ N$, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K(\!(X)\!)$ over $K$ generated by the two $q$-expansions `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`. A place of this field over $K$ is, in the sense of the structure [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22), a valuation subring of it that contains the image of $K$, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring. The assertion is that the set $\mathtt{ssPlaces}\ q\ N\ K$ of those places $w$ which satisfy the three conditions defining `IsSupersingularPlace` — $w$ is rational (the predicate `Place.IsRational`), $w$ satisfies the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace K N`, and the value $w(\,\mathtt{jGeomGen}\ K\ N\,)$ of the geometric $j$-generator at $w$ lies in the set $\mathtt{ssJSet}\ q\ K$ — is a finite subset of the set of places.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the set of supersingular points in characteristic $q$ on the level-$N$ modular curve, in the function-field formulation used throughout the project. It is invoked by the Čerednik–Drinfeld material and by the level-structure Tate-module computations, where sums and products indexed by supersingular places must be taken over a finite index set.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ssPlaces_finite.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SupersingularNodePlaces

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
